  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of first four terms of a geometric progression <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>65</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math> and the sum of their respective reciprocals is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>65</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> If the product of first three terms of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> and the third term is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is _________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let number are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>65</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>65</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>65</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So, third term<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>"
  }
